From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: rk8xx: leave the RK817 RTC running

The RK817 init table stops the RTC (RTC_STOP in RK817_RTC_CTRL_REG) when
the MFD probes; the RTC driver starts it again when it probes. With the
MFD built in and rtc-rk808 a module, every boot lost the time between the
two, and a resume from hibernation lost it for good: the boot kernel that
loads the image stops the RTC, and the restored kernel never probes the
RTC driver again. On the ODROID-GO Ultra the battery-backed clock then
stood still until it was set (read as 02:11:20 for hours).

The RK808 and RK818 tables have no such entry, and rtc-rk808 clears the
stop bit itself at probe: drop it.

--- a/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
@@ -204,7 +204,6 @@
 };
 
 static const struct rk808_reg_data rk817_pre_init_reg[] = {
-	{RK817_RTC_CTRL_REG, RTC_STOP, RTC_STOP},
 	/* Codec specific registers */
 	{ RK817_CODEC_DTOP_VUCTL, MASK_ALL, 0x03 },
 	{ RK817_CODEC_DTOP_VUCTIME, MASK_ALL, 0x00 },
